SPECIFICATION Goldring1042_PhysicalBehaviour VERSION 1.0
DATE 2026-11-22
PURPOSE "Component contract for CAD planning, model identification and future simulation."
STATUS "Geometry audited; physical specimen not identified; no executable simulator."

// This is language-neutral pseudocode. REQUIRE rejects an unsupported operation.
// UNKNOWN is epistemic absence, not zero, infinity, a default material or a random value.
// EQUATION states a physical/model relation, not an implemented numerical solver.
// MODEL_CHOICE must name assumptions and its validity domain in every result.
// A function declared here is a required interface, not an existing implementation.
// References Mxx/Ixx/Oxx/C01/D01 resolve through the permanent source links below.
// Sharing copy: only source-reference locations differ from the workbench specification.

IMPORT evidence_register FROM "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Engrove/turntable-workbench/980695086ed349739fc9ec5eb7e4dfcc1238a568/assets/cartridges/goldring-1042/analysis/REV_D_physical_model/sources.json"
IMPORT parameters FROM "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Engrove/turntable-workbench/980695086ed349739fc9ec5eb7e4dfcc1238a568/assets/cartridges/goldring-1042/analysis/REV_D_physical_model/physical_parameters.json"
IMPORT historical_observations FROM "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Engrove/turntable-workbench/980695086ed349739fc9ec5eb7e4dfcc1238a568/assets/cartridges/goldring-1042/analysis/REV_D_physical_model/measurements.json"
IMPORT CAD_audit FROM "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Engrove/turntable-workbench/980695086ed349739fc9ec5eb7e4dfcc1238a568/assets/cartridges/goldring-1042/analysis/REV_D_physical_model/geometry_audit.json"

TYPE EvidenceQuantity<T>:
    value: T OR UNKNOWN
    unit: dimensionally_explicit_unit
    status: MANUFACTURER_NOMINAL | INDEPENDENT_REPORT | CAD_EXACT
            | ANALYTICALLY_DERIVED | SCENARIO | UNKNOWN
    source_ids: set<string>
    specimen_id: string OR UNKNOWN
    conditions: {frequency, temperature, VTF, direction, amplitude_convention,
                 record, load, instrument, calibration, age, mounting}
    uncertainty: distribution_or_interval OR UNKNOWN
    applicability: explicit_domain
    correlation_group: string OR UNKNOWN

RULES Evidence:
    CAD_EXACT does not imply PHYSICALLY_MEASURED.
    MANUFACTURER_NOMINAL does not imply ACTUAL_SPECIMEN_VALUE.
    An independent report without uncertainty is not traceable calibration.
    I01 and I02 share author/laboratory lineage; never count as two replications.
    Never average incompatible source profiles or unidentified specimens.
    Never treat source conflict as a statistical confidence interval.
    Never infer damping, friction or centre of mass from a rendered surface.
    Never infer physical material identity from a CAD part name or render colour.
    A failed specimen is not a calibration sample for normal operation.
    Every prediction retains input provenance and MODEL_CHOICE assumptions.

UNITS:
    internal = {metre, kilogram, second, newton, radian, volt, ampere, ohm, henry, farad}
    CAD_mm_to_m = 0.001
    gram_to_kg = 0.001
    milligram_to_kg = 0.000001
    gram_force_to_N = 0.00980665
    mm_per_N_to_m_per_N = 0.001
    micrometre_per_millinewton == millimetre_per_newton
    pF_to_F = 1e-12
    mH_to_H = 0.001
    degree_to_radian = PI / 180
    rpm_to_rad_s = 2 * PI / 60

FRAMES:
    C = right_handed_cartridge_frame
        origin = nominal_CAD_stylus_apex
        ex = toward_rear_terminals
        ey = transverse_axis_defined_by_CAD
        ez = upwards_from_nominal_record_plane
    M = mounting_datum_frame
        orientation = C.orientation
        origin_in_C = [10.2, 0, 17.3] mm
    W = inertial_world_frame
    G = local_record_groove_frame
        ex = local_groove_tangent
        ey = local_lateral_direction
        ez = local_record_normal
        REQUIRE orientation is right_handed
    R_WC = proper_rotation_matrix
    r_WC = C_origin_in_W
    T_WC(point_C) = r_WC + R_WC * point_C
    p_M = p_C - [10.2, 0, 17.3] mm
    glTF_point_m = [CAD_x, CAD_z, -CAD_y] * 0.001
    REQUIRE determinant(R_WC) == +1 within numerical tolerance

GEOMETRIC_DATUMS:
    nominal_tip_C = [0, 0, 0] mm
    mounting_hole_centres_C = [[10.2,-6.35,17.3], [10.2,+6.35,17.3]] mm
    nominal_mount_plane_C = z=17.3 mm
    mount_spacing = 12.7 mm                         // M01, M02
    tip_to_hole_longitudinal = 10.2 mm              // M03
    nominal_mount_to_tip_height = 17.3 mm           // M03; M01 also states 17 mm
    datum_loading_condition = UNKNOWN
    mount_through_hole_diameter_CAD = 2.8 mm        // C01 only
    nominal_supplied_screws = M2.5 x 8 mm with nuts // M06
    mounting_torque = UNKNOWN
    terminal_diameter_nominal = 1.2 mm              // M08
    real_tolerance_of_each_datum = UNKNOWN
    real_loaded_tip_location = UNKNOWN

GEOMETRY_SCOPE:
    audited_visual_parts = 24
    audited_solids = 40
    CAD_bounds_mm = [[-3.1,-8.7,0], [25.2,8.7,17.3]]
    CAD_flange_dimensions_mm = [17.6,17.4,2.4]
    CAD_shell_to_nominal_plane_clearance_mm = 1.075072748
    CAD_stylus_seam_nominal_gap_mm = 0.075
    CAD_cantilever_visible_length_mm = 4.531794193
    CAD_cantilever_outer_inner_diameter_mm = [0.30,0.20]
    CAD_diamond_shape = CONICAL_VISUAL_PROXY
    real_Gyger_S_surface = UNKNOWN
    visual_overlap_pairs = 19
    physical_mass = UNKNOWN                        // source nominal masses below
    physical_COM = UNKNOWN
    physical_inertia_tensor = UNKNOWN
    detailed_part_geometry = CAD_audit.parts
    RULE visual shells contain invented/omitted internal volumes.
    RULE summed CAD volume and its centroid are not physical mass properties.
    RULE tiny cone apex is not a physically valid contact-pressure surface.
    RULE D42 visual seam is not a calibrated disassembly trajectory or latch.
    RULE connector lugs, cables, screw heads, nuts and tool clearance require
         additional assembly geometry; they are absent from this cartridge file.

ASSEMBLY physical_topology:
    FIXED_GROUP body:
        mounting_flange -> headshell_via_two_screws_and_nuts
        material_identity = glass_reinforced_Pocan_polyester          // M01
        structural_density_modulus_loss_tensor = UNKNOWN
        generator_shield = mu_metal_can                             // M01
        pole_pieces = laminated_mu_metal                            // M01
        coils = two_fixed_formerless_coils                          // M01
        stated_turns_per_coil = 4000                                // M01
        winding_wire_geometry_and_losses = UNKNOWN
        four_rear_terminals -> two_electrical_output_ports
        terminal_contact_resistance_and_strength = UNKNOWN
    REMOVABLE_GROUP D42:
        housing -> seats_in_body_with_locating_feature              // M01
        seat_stiffness_damping_clearance = UNKNOWN
        suspension = butyl_rubber_polymer                          // M01
        moving_magnet = Alnico_V                                   // M01
        tie_bar = gold_plated_nickel                                // M01
        tie_bar_roles = [mechanical_constraint, electrical_charge_path]
        cantilever = aluminium                                     // M01
        stylus = nude_diamond_with_Gyger_S_cut                       // M01
        actual_geometry_mass_distribution_magnetic_circuit = UNKNOWN
    ON_REMOVE D42:
        nominal_groove_to_generator_conversion = unavailable
        body_coils_and_their_electrical_noise_remain
        external_field_pickup_may_remain
    RULE CAD brass sleeve / tie bar names are visual modelling hypotheses;
         they do not override manufacturer's material description.

SOURCE_PROFILES:
    CURRENT_WEB_M01:
        total_cartridge_mass_nominal = 0.0062 kg
        total_mass_with_supplied_fixings_nominal = 0.0076 kg
        coil_R_nominal = 820 ohm
        coil_L_nominal = 0.470 H
        effective_tip_mass_nominal = 3.5e-7 kg
        sensitivity_nominal = 0.005 V at lateral_velocity=0.05 m/s
        sensitivity_tolerance = +/-3 dB
        nominal_VTF = 1.75 gram_force
        external_C_recommendation = [125e-12,225e-12] F
        nominal_external_C = 175e-12 F
    LEGACY_SHEET_M02:
        total_cartridge_mass_nominal = 0.0063 kg
        total_mass_with_supplied_fixings_nominal = 0.0076 kg
        coil_R_nominal = 660 ohm
        coil_L_nominal = 0.570 H
        effective_tip_mass_nominal = 4.5e-7 kg
        sensitivity_nominal = 0.0065 V at 1000 Hz and velocity=0.05 m/s
        sensitivity_tolerance = +/-1.5 dB
        nominal_VTF = 1.7 gram_force
        external_C_recommendation = [150e-12,200e-12] F
    COMMON:
        VTF_operating_range = [1.5,2.0] gram_force
        external_R_recommendation = 47000 ohm
        static_C_lateral_nominal = 0.024 m/N
        static_C_vertical_nominal = 0.016 m/N
        dynamic_C_10Hz_claims = [0.010..0.012 from M05, 0.013 from M04] m/N
        dynamic_C_axis_phase_and_test_amplitude = UNKNOWN
        nominal_VTA = 24 degree
    USER_SPECIMEN:
        selected_profile = UNIDENTIFIED
        REQUIRE measured_mass_and_electrical_impedance_and_identity
                before labelling a profile as specimen-calibrated
        RULE differences may be editorial, methodological or physical;
             a documented hardware revision change has not been established.
        RULE equivalent tip mass is a reduced-model parameter, not diamond mass.
        RULE do not add tip mass twice when partitioning total assembly mass.

ANGLE_DEFINITIONS:
    azimuth = roll_of_stylus_sensitive_axes_relative_to_local_groove
    zenith_or_horizontal_tracking_error = yaw_relative_to_groove_tangent
    VTA = angle_associated_with_effective_vertical_tracking_motion
    SRA = rake_angle_of_actual_contact_edge_relative_to_record
    cantilever_angle = visible_cantilever_axis_inclination
    diamond_shank_angle = visible_diamond_body_orientation
    RULE these six quantities are distinct.
    RULE CAD cantilever 24 degrees does not establish real VTA or SRA.
    RULE M07 describes an intentionally forward-inclined Gyger shank;
         do not tilt the whole cartridge merely to make that shank vertical.

PORTS:
    mechanical_mount_port:
        input = pose, twist, acceleration OR external_support_constraints
        output = wrench_at_named_mount_datum
        no_overconstraint = do_not_prescribe_pose_and_independent_net_force
    groove_port:
        input = two_wall_surfaces_in_W, record_material_state, record_motion
        output = wall_reaction_forces, friction_forces, contact_state
    lead_wire_port:
        input = harness_pose_velocity_and_characterised_force_law
        output = wrench_on_body, electrical_RLC_and_microphonic_effects
    electrical_ports:
        L = differential(L_plus_white, L_minus_blue)
        R = differential(R_plus_red, R_minus_green)
        ground_network = UNKNOWN
        REQUIRE actual_pin_markings_or_continuity for physical wiring
        RULE CAD spatial positions are not wiring certification.
    environmental_ports:
        input = gravity, temperature, humidity, external_magnetic_field,
                airborne_or_structure_vibration, contamination, elapsed_time
        output = state-dependent response OR explicit NOT_IDENTIFIED

STATE:
    rigid_body_pose_and_twist
    moving_subsystem_generalized_coordinates q
    moving_subsystem_generalized_velocities q_dot
    viscoelastic_internal_states z_j
    coil_currents i[2]
    terminal_voltages v[2]
    contact_status_per_wall
    stylus_seated: TRUE | FALSE | UNKNOWN
    protective_guard_status: ABSENT | FITTED | UNKNOWN
    wear_and_damage_state
    temperature_and_charge_states_if_modelled
    parameter_profile_and_uncertainty

MODEL_CHOICE LowFrequencyRelativeCoordinates:
    q = [lateral_displacement_y, vertical_displacement_z] in metre
    reference = explicitly_measured_equilibrium_at_specified_VTF_and_temperature
    REQUIRE q=0 is not silently equated to unloaded CAD tip datum
    extension = optional_fore_aft_and_rotational_bending_modes_with_declared_units
    tip_C(q) = calibrated_reference_tip_C + B_tip * q + higher_order_kinematics(q)
    tip_W = T_WC(tip_C(q))
    tip_velocity_W = body_translation_velocity
                     + body_omega CROSS (R_WC * tip_C(q))
                     + R_WC * tip_jacobian(q) * q_dot
    RULE effective moving mass and B_tip must use the same modal normalization.

MODEL_CHOICE PassiveViscoelasticSuspension:
    // One possible identification model, not known Goldring coefficients.
    restoring_force = K0*q + SUM_j[Kj*(q-z_j)] + C0*q_dot
                      + nonlinear_elastic_force(q,preload,T,age)
                      + nonlinear_dissipative_force(q,q_dot,T,age)
    z_j_dot = (q-z_j)/tau_j
    REQUIRE K0 and Kj symmetric_positive_semidefinite
    REQUIRE C0 symmetric_positive_semidefinite and tau_j > 0
    REQUIRE nonlinear_loss_power >= 0 in validated_domain
    REQUIRE coefficient_values identified; UNKNOWN is not zero
    small_signal_dynamic_stiffness(omega) =
        K0 + SUM_j[Kj*(j*omega*tau_j)/(1+j*omega*tau_j)] + j*omega*C0
    compliance_matrix(omega) = inverse(small_signal_dynamic_stiffness(omega))
    RULE inertial tip transfer is not the same as suspension compliance.
    RULE published scalar compliance may use a different test convention;
         measurement operator must match before fitting the model.
    RULE static_C_lateral and static_C_vertical do not identify Kj or tau_j.
    RULE a single 10 Hz scalar does not identify anisotropy, phase or damping.

EQUATIONS CoupledMechanics:
    // Preferred full assembly form includes body, arm links and moving stylus.
    M(Q)*Q_ddot + h(Q,Q_dot) + internal_restoring_and_loss(Q,Q_dot,z) =
        Q_gravity + Q_applied + J_mount_transpose*wrench_mount
        + J_contact_transpose*contact_forces
        + Q_electromagnetic + Q_wire
    position_constraints(Q,time) = 0
    velocity_constraints = constraint_J*Q_dot + explicit_time_derivative = 0
    REQUIRE a consistent mass partition, units and reference frame for every term
    REQUIRE supplied arm linkage geometry for Engrove LT
    RULE do not substitute a fixed-pivot arm or generic offset angle for LT.
    RULE enforce constraints using a suitable DAE/contact method, not animation.
    RULE a prescribed-arm motion model predicts reactions, not free arm motion.

    // Equivalent body wrench balance, if the moving subsystem is separate:
    m_body * a_COM = F_mount + m_body*g + F_from_moving_system + F_wire + F_other
    I_COM*omega_dot + omega CROSS (I_COM*omega) = total_torque_at_COM
    wrench_at_M = shift_wrench(wrench_at_COM, COM_minus_M)
    shift_wrench([F,tau], r) = [F, tau + r CROSS F]
    REQUIRE m_body excludes explicitly modelled moving mass
    REQUIRE I_COM and r_COM identified for quantitative rigid-body response

STATIC_INITIALISATION:
    assemble_arm_and_cartridge_in_gravity
    apply_counterbalance_and_tracking_force_mechanism
    solve_equilibrium_with_contact_and_suspension_preload
    VTF_measured = upward_resultant_contact_force_projected_on_record_normal
    REQUIRE desired_VTF matches computed_or_measured_equilibrium
    RULE cartridge_weight alone is not tracking force.
    RULE do not add a separate VTF force if arm gravity/bias already produces it.
    RULE CAD 17.3 mm load condition is unknown.
    conditional_example:
        F_at_1_75gf = 0.0171616375 N
        unloaded_linear_deflection = 0.016 m/N * F_at_1_75gf
                                   = 0.0002745862 m
        validity = linear_static_spring_and_known_unloaded_zero_only
        prohibition = never_auto_subtract_from_17_3mm_height

CONTACT two_wall_groove:
    // Ideal symmetric 90-degree V-groove example. Actual surfaces may differ.
    n_L_G = [0,+1,+1]/sqrt(2)
    n_R_G = [0,-1,+1]/sqrt(2)
    FOR wall IN [L,R]:
        signed_gap[wall] >= 0
        normal_force[wall] >= 0
        signed_gap[wall] * normal_force[wall] = 0
        contact_point = support_point(actual_tip_surface, actual_wall_surface)
        tangential_relative_velocity = tip_velocity - wall_velocity
                                      projected_into_wall_tangent_plane
        friction_force = identified_friction_law(normal_force,
                         tangential_relative_velocity,T,contamination,wear)
        REQUIRE friction_force DOT tangential_relative_velocity <= 0
    symmetric_static_example:
        N_L = N_R = VTF / sqrt(2)
        SUM_normal_magnitudes = sqrt(2) * VTF
        Coulomb_tangential_drag = mu * sqrt(2) * VTF
        REQUIRE identical_mu_and_symmetric_contact
    RULE mu is UNKNOWN; the example is not a measured drag prediction.
    RULE a blank disc and a two-wall groove have different force geometry.
    RULE loss of one wall is distinct from complete loss of contact.
    RULE no tensile normal reaction may hold the stylus inside a groove.
    RULE local contact compliance and the cartridge suspension are separate.
    RULE the visual cone cannot provide finite Gyger contact pressure.
    contact_pressure_or_wear_request:
        REQUIRE real_tip_curvatures, real_wall_profile, material_response,
                force_history, friction_and_wear_calibration
        OTHERWISE RETURN NOT_IDENTIFIED

ARM_AND_RECORD_COUPLING:
    record_angle_dot = supplied_actual_omega(time)
    local_surface_speed = radius * record_angle_dot
    local_modulation_wavelength = local_surface_speed / modulation_frequency
    groove_surfaces = authored_spiral + encoded_modulation + measured_warp
                      + measured_eccentricity + surface_defects
    body_clearance = signed_distance(actual_body_geometry, moving_record_surface)
    REQUIRE loaded_geometry_and_tolerances for real collision certification
    stylus_drag_wrench = [F_drag, (tip_position-reference_point) CROSS F_drag]
    LT_generalized_drag_force = actual_LT_contact_J_transpose * F_drag
    RULE no universal inward skating torque or fixed antiskate fraction.
    RULE wire stiffness, bearing friction and constraint geometry can bias LT.
    RULE groove speed changes with radius even at constant rpm.
    RULE warp and eccentricity excite arm/suspension, not just the visual mesh.
    RULE do not resample away platter-speed or centering error being studied.

STEREO_KINEMATICS ideal_convention:
    B_45 = [[1,1],[1,-1]] / sqrt(2)
    wall_signal_coordinates = B_45 * [lateral_y,vertical_z]
    pure_lateral_motion -> equal_sign_channels
    pure_vertical_motion -> opposite_sign_channels
    REQUIRE physical_terminal_polarity_verified
    azimuth_yaw_pitch_transform = measured_rotation_between_C_and_G
    RULE mechanical misalignment and intrinsic generator crosstalk are distinct.
    RULE do not apply B_45 again if calibrated G already includes channel axes.

MODEL_CHOICE ReciprocalSmallSignalGenerator:
    // Sign convention: i flows OUT of the generator into the external load.
    // G maps chosen mechanical coordinates directly to terminal polarities.
    open_circuit_emf e = G * q_dot
    electromagnetic_force_on_moving_system = -transpose(G) * i
    coil_equation: L * i_dot + R * i + v = e
    external_parallel_RC_load: C_ext * v_dot + inverse(R_load) * v = i
    REQUIRE compatible SI units: G in V*s/m = N/A for displacement coordinates
    REQUIRE R and L physically admissible matrices, declared mutual coupling
    REQUIRE G and electrical_parameters fitted for the same specimen/domain
    mechanical_conversion_power = -q_dot DOT transpose(G)*i = -e DOT i
    electrical_received_power = e DOT i
    RULE conversion conserves power; resistive/mechanical losses dissipate it.
    RULE magnetostriction, hysteresis, eddy-current and distributed winding
         effects require added causal passive states or measured frequency model.
    RULE manufacturer output sensitivity is not automatically intrinsic G;
         loading, mechanical transfer and velocity conventions may be included.
    RULE do not multiply by a measured complete transfer and then repeat its
         mechanical/electrical loading factors a second time.

MODEL_CHOICE SingleChannelElectricalApproximation:
    Z_coil(omega) = R_coil + j*omega*L_coil
    C_ext = C_arm_leads + C_interconnect + C_phono_input + external_stray_C
    Z_load(omega) = 1 / (1/R_load + j*omega*C_ext)
    H_electrical(omega) = Z_load / (Z_coil + Z_load)
    H_total = H_mechanical * G_velocity_conversion * H_electrical
    RULE self_capacitance_of_coil is separate and UNKNOWN, not silently zero
         in a claimed full-band accurate model.
    lossless_LC_reference_frequency = 1/(2*PI*sqrt(L_coil*C_ext))
    RULE LC reference is not guaranteed measured treble-peak frequency.
    RULE I02 reports approximate peaks at 16 kHz / 80 pF and 10 kHz / 380 pF;
         these constrain a historical combined response, not L alone.
    RULE RIAA playback equalisation and preamp overload belong downstream.
    RULE a test record may already encode frequency compensation;
         inspect its specification before de-embedding or applying RIAA.

NOISE_AND_INTERFERENCE:
    resistor_thermal_voltage_PSD = 4 * Boltzmann_constant * temperature_K * R
    REQUIRE temperature_and_network_transfer for output noise integration
    total_noise = filtered_resistor_noise + measured_magnetic_noise
                  + mechanical_thermal_noise + groove_surface_noise
                  + cable_microphonics + preamp_noise
    REQUIRE correlation_cross_spectra where sources are not independent
    external_B_field -> coil_emf_and_shield_response
    relative_body_vibration -> cantilever_motion -> generated_voltage
    static_charge -> measured_ground_path_and_discharge_behaviour
    RULE shield effectiveness and ground topology are UNKNOWN quantitatively.

OPTIONAL_HIGHER_ORDER_PHYSICS:
    housing_flexure_and_mount_modes -> identified_structural_modal_model
    magnetic_nonlinearity_and_saturation -> characterised_field_and_force_law
    thermal_expansion_and_rubber_aging -> identified_temperature_time_dependence
    aerodynamic_or_electrostatic_forces -> quantified_external_field_model
    finite_contact_temperature_and_wear -> validated_tribological_model
    RULE omission requires a scope statement or bounded sensitivity argument;
         absence of data is not evidence that an effect is physically zero.

FREQUENCY_AND_TRACKING_OBSERVABLES:
    transfer_matrix H(f) = output_voltage_vector / declared_stimulus_vector
    balance_dB = 20*log10(abs(H_LL/H_RR)) under matching channel excitation
    separation_L_dB = 20*log10(abs(H_LL/H_RL)) for left_only_excitation
    separation_R_dB = 20*log10(abs(H_RR/H_LR)) for right_only_excitation
    RULE one separation magnitude cannot determine complex off-diagonal terms.
    RULE nominal 25 dB and historical 22 dB are not interchangeable assertions.
    tracking_limit = amplitude_at_predeclared_distortion_or_contact_loss_criterion
    REQUIRE frequency, direction, peak_RMS_or_peak_to_peak, VTF, record,
            temperature, load and distortion_metric
    RULE I01 lateral 90 um and vertical 45 um at 300 Hz do not describe all audio.
    RULE manufacturer's 80 um lacks sufficient conditions for a universal limit.
    RULE no hardcoded pass/fail threshold based only on displacement amplitude.

MODEL_CHOICE SimpleOneAxisResonanceScenario:
    f_approx = 1/(2*PI*sqrt((arm_effective_mass+cartridge_mass+hardware_mass)
                           * dynamic_compliance))
    REQUIRE all mass terms in kg and compliance in m/N
    REQUIRE a one-axis tip-referred lumped model with declared mass convention
    scenarios_C_10Hz = [0.010,0.012,0.013] m/N
    RULE these are source-conflict scenarios, not measured uncertainty bounds.
    RULE do not substitute static 0.024 m/N for dynamic compliance.
    RULE frequency-dependent compliance makes the resonance condition implicit.
    RULE actual LT modal frequencies come from its constrained mass/stiffness
         system; this scalar scenario is not the LT design acceptance criterion.

OPERATING_STATE_MACHINE:
    STORAGE -> guard_removed_and_assembly_checked -> INSTALLED_UNVERIFIED
    ASSEMBLY_ABSENT -> require_D42_installation -> INSTALLED_UNVERIFIED
    INSTALLED_UNVERIFIED -> seating_and_identity_verified -> RAISED
    RAISED -> lowering_and_first_contact -> SETTLING
    SETTLING -> equilibrium_and_two_wall_contact -> TRACKING
    TRACKING -> one_normal_force_zero_with_opening_gap -> ONE_WALL_LOSS
    ONE_WALL_LOSS -> both_gaps_open -> AIRBORNE
    ONE_WALL_LOSS or AIRBORNE -> recontact -> IMPACT_AND_SETTLING
    TRACKING -> measured_suspension_stop_reached -> BOTTOMED_OR_LIMITED
    any_lowered_state -> body_record_intersection -> BODY_CONTACT
    any_contact_state -> lift_command -> UNLOADING -> RAISED
    any_state -> D42_removed -> ASSEMBLY_ABSENT
    any_state -> damage_or_wear_evidence -> DEGRADED_OR_FAULTY
    any_state -> terminal_open_short_or_ground_fault -> ELECTRICAL_FAULT
    electrical_fault_state may coexist with mechanical tracking state
    long_term_aging_and_contamination may change parameters in every state
    REQUIRE thresholds and impact law identified before predicting transitions
    REQUIRE protective_guard_status == ABSENT before tracking operation
    RULE reporting a possible event is different from predicting its threshold.
    RULE O01 supports a removable-assembly fault scenario, not an exact failure cause.

FUTURE_SOLVER_CONTRACT step(inputs, state, requested_fidelity):
    validate_units_frames_profile_and_provenance()
    missing = required_unknowns(requested_fidelity, inputs, state)
    IF missing not empty:
        RETURN {status: NOT_IDENTIFIED, missing_parameters: missing,
                available_lower_fidelity_modes: explicitly_listed_modes}
    establish_consistent_initial_conditions_and_constraints()
    determine_record_and_mount_kinematics_from_supplied_geometry()
    solve_coupled_mechanical_electrical_contact_equations()
    update_event_states_without_allowing_negative_normal_reactions()
    check_energy_balance_passivity_and_numerical_convergence()
    RETURN {
        status: PREDICTION_WITH_DECLARED_SCOPE,
        tip_pose, body_pose, mounting_wrench, contact_forces, contact_state,
        suspension_deflection, output_voltage, channel_transfer_if_excited,
        collision_margins_if_geometry_valid, model_validity_flags,
        uncertainty_if_identified_else_UNKNOWN,
        source_profile, specimen_id, assumptions, calibration_domain
    }

IDENTIFICATION_AND_ACCEPTANCE:
    preserve all raw observations with specimen and instrument metadata
    measure actual electrical R/L/complex impedance and complete external load
    measure mass, loaded datums, COM and inertia where requested physics needs them
    identify lateral and vertical complex compliance over relevant force/frequency range
    use independent holdout conditions, not the same observations used for fitting
    verify monotonic load-peak shift against I02 qualitatively, unless replicating its setup
    compare I01 numerical anchors only when stimulus conventions are resolved
    do not force current specimen to match a 1993 sample
    quarantine O01 from healthy-transfer parameter estimation
    verify mono polarity, channel separation and grounding independently of CAD
    verify passivity, dimensional consistency and energy balance
    document unidentifiable parameter combinations instead of inventing unique values
    promote a capability only when its required inputs and validation are available
    never report PERFECT_DIGITAL_TWIN from sparse specifications and photographs

END SPECIFICATION
